1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,301
Imagine a clinician reviewing a long ECG
recording.

2
00:00:04,301 --> 00:00:08,690
Detecting atrial fibrillation after it
begins is one question.

3
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:14,542
Our question is harder: could the
preceding signal support a warning before

4
00:00:14,542 --> 00:00:16,492
a new episode starts?

5
00:00:16,492 --> 00:00:22,344
CardioTwin is a research prototype for
that question, built for the CRP

6
00:00:22,344 --> 00:00:27,220
Digital Twin Challenge by Team Lazarus
from MGM's Jawaharlal Nehru

7
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:28,196
Engineering College.

8
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:33,072
It combines historical ECG, permitted
patient context, persistent state and

9
00:00:33,072 --> 00:00:34,535
a review dashboard.

10
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:40,387
The practical idea is to make a future
warning inspectable rather than

11
00:00:40,387 --> 00:00:42,337
display an unexplained number.

12
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:48,189
The intended output is a reviewable
warning, with evidence and an explicit

13
00:00:48,189 --> 00:00:49,164
availability reason.

14
00:00:49,826 --> 00:00:56,666
Here is the result early: the frozen
finalist caught six of two hundred and

15
00:00:56,666 --> 00:01:01,063
forty-one development events, one of
forty-three primary held-out events,

16
00:01:01,063 --> 00:01:03,995
and two of twenty-nine external events.

17
00:01:03,995 --> 00:01:09,858
These results miss our own fifty percent
sensitivity target by a wide

18
00:01:09,858 --> 00:01:10,347
margin.

19
00:01:10,347 --> 00:01:15,721
We are presenting a functioning research
workflow and an honest negative

20
00:01:15,721 --> 00:01:16,210
finding.

21
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:20,119
A working interface does not establish
useful forecasting.

22
00:01:20,119 --> 00:01:25,982
Later, we will explain why even a low
false-warning rate needs careful

23
00:01:25,982 --> 00:01:26,470
interpretation.

24
00:01:27,132 --> 00:01:33,652
The intended use case matters in India,
but we have no Indian recordings or

25
00:01:33,652 --> 00:01:34,584
local validation.

26
00:01:34,584 --> 00:01:39,707
We therefore make no claim about Indian
performance, clinical benefit or

27
00:01:39,707 --> 00:01:40,172
deployment.

28
00:01:40,172 --> 00:01:44,364
Public retrospective data can help
investigate an engineering question;

29
00:01:44,364 --> 00:01:49,487
they cannot substitute for evidence from
the population and care setting

30
00:01:49,487 --> 00:01:52,747
where a tool would actually be used.

31
00:01:52,747 --> 00:01:57,405
Clinical review and prospective evaluation
would be separate future work.

32
00:01:58,066 --> 00:02:04,321
Our fixed contract uses the preceding ten
minutes of ECG, with one decision

33
00:02:04,321 --> 00:02:11,537
every thirty seconds, to try to forecast a
new AF onset two to ten minutes

34
00:02:11,537 --> 00:02:12,018
ahead.

35
00:02:12,018 --> 00:02:15,867
It is not a heart-attack or stroke
forecast.

36
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:20,197
During this video, manufactured dashboard
examples demonstrate the software.

37
00:02:20,197 --> 00:02:23,565
Saved real-data evaluations establish the
weak results.

38
00:02:23,565 --> 00:02:29,339
Keeping those two forms of evidence
separate is central to the project.

39
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:34,121
Follow the online path from left to right.

40
00:02:34,121 --> 00:02:38,308
The replay service advances historical ECG
in thirty-second ticks.

41
00:02:38,308 --> 00:02:43,889
At each decision it reads only the
preceding ten minutes, extracts features,

42
00:02:43,889 --> 00:02:46,215
and applies shared signal-quality checks.

43
00:02:46,215 --> 00:02:52,262
It builds the feature row from the
previous patient baseline, scores it with

44
00:02:52,262 --> 00:02:55,518
frozen model weights, then updates the
baseline.

45
00:02:55,518 --> 00:02:59,704
An alert state machine applies
persistence, hysteresis and cooldown.

46
00:02:59,704 --> 00:03:04,821
Cursor, baseline, alert state and warning
are committed together in SQLite.

47
00:03:04,821 --> 00:03:08,542
FastAPI exposes that state, and React
renders it.

48
00:03:08,542 --> 00:03:13,659
Restarting the service should continue
from the saved cursor rather than

49
00:03:13,659 --> 00:03:15,054
repeat a decision.

50
00:03:15,054 --> 00:03:17,845
Each patient keeps separate replay state.

51
00:03:18,491 --> 00:03:24,219
The offline path answers a different
question: did warnings arrive before

52
00:03:24,219 --> 00:03:25,781
real annotated events?

53
00:03:25,781 --> 00:03:30,468
Annotation-derived future labels belong in
training and evaluation, never

54
00:03:30,468 --> 00:03:32,551
among runtime predictor inputs.

55
00:03:32,551 --> 00:03:37,238
Patient groups are separated before
fitting, calibration and policy

56
00:03:37,238 --> 00:03:37,758
selection.

57
00:03:37,758 --> 00:03:42,445
Model packages bind their configuration,
feature schema and checksums.

58
00:03:42,445 --> 00:03:47,653
Complete chronological evaluation then
uses the same alert implementation as

59
00:03:47,653 --> 00:03:52,860
replay, so our reported policy is tied to
executable behavior.

60
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:56,505
A saved test-access ledger records
evaluation use;

61
00:03:56,505 --> 00:04:00,150
it does not magically certify historical
blinding.

62
00:04:00,796 --> 00:04:05,132
The challenge asks for static and dynamic
data fusion.

63
00:04:05,132 --> 00:04:10,912
The real static stream contains paired age
and sex from IRIDIA-AF metadata.

64
00:04:10,912 --> 00:04:14,766
We did not invent diagnoses or laboratory
values.

65
00:04:14,766 --> 00:04:19,101
The dynamic stream contains twenty-three
causal ECG features describing

66
00:04:19,101 --> 00:04:22,473
heart rate, RR variability and recent
changes.

67
00:04:22,473 --> 00:04:27,290
The frozen logistic finalist has
twenty-seven named inputs: those ECG

68
00:04:27,290 --> 00:04:31,144
features, age, sex and their two
availability flags.

69
00:04:31,144 --> 00:04:33,552
Missing values are handled explicitly.

70
00:04:33,552 --> 00:04:39,815
The running personal baseline is
persistent twin state, but it is not an

71
00:04:39,815 --> 00:04:41,741
input to this finalist.

72
00:04:41,741 --> 00:04:45,113
Some exploratory model variants used
baseline features;

73
00:04:45,113 --> 00:04:48,485
that does not change the finalist's
schema.

74
00:04:48,485 --> 00:04:53,302
Our ECG-only reference tests whether
adding age and sex helped.

75
00:04:53,948 --> 00:04:58,254
That distinction defines our digital twin:
a patient-specific historical

76
00:04:58,254 --> 00:05:03,517
state and inspectable replay, not a
simulated anatomical heart and not

77
00:05:03,517 --> 00:05:04,953
continuous model retraining.

78
00:05:04,953 --> 00:05:10,216
The code supports more clinical fields
than the real cohort supplies.

79
00:05:10,216 --> 00:05:14,522
Manufactured profiles exercise parts of
the interface without becoming

80
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:16,914
evidence of richer real-world fusion.

81
00:05:16,914 --> 00:05:19,785
The comparison found no fusion benefit.

82
00:05:19,785 --> 00:05:24,570
We preserve that conclusion alongside the
software capability, rather than

83
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:29,354
infer better prediction from the presence
of two input streams.

84
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:34,894
This dashboard footage uses manufactured
ECG and manufactured clinical

85
00:05:34,894 --> 00:05:38,888
profiles, with a model trained on
synthetic examples.

86
00:05:38,888 --> 00:05:42,384
It demonstrates software behavior, not
patient performance.

87
00:05:42,384 --> 00:05:47,876
The normal server refuses the real
finalist because it failed acceptance

88
00:05:47,876 --> 00:05:48,375
gates.

89
00:05:48,375 --> 00:05:54,367
An explicit research mode exists, with a
red warning banner, but no

90
00:05:54,367 --> 00:05:57,862
real-record replay is shown in this video.

91
00:05:57,862 --> 00:06:01,857
The real-data results appear separately in
saved reports.

92
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:06,352
Start with the patient selector and
record-relative clock.

93
00:06:06,352 --> 00:06:12,114
The recent ECG panel displays the last ten
seconds, while prediction uses

94
00:06:12,114 --> 00:06:14,034
the preceding ten minutes.

95
00:06:14,034 --> 00:06:17,395
Heart-rate and RR trends summarize earlier
decisions.

96
00:06:17,395 --> 00:06:20,756
The patient-context panel contains
manufactured values here;

97
00:06:20,756 --> 00:06:25,078
the real IRIDIA cohort supplies age and
sex only.

98
00:06:25,078 --> 00:06:28,439
The displayed ECG is downsampled for
readability;

99
00:06:28,439 --> 00:06:33,241
it is not the exact array used for feature
extraction.

100
00:06:33,241 --> 00:06:38,042
Displaying fewer points is a presentation
choice, while prediction still

101
00:06:38,042 --> 00:06:41,403
uses the complete specified trailing
signal window.

102
00:06:41,403 --> 00:06:46,205
Source sampling rate, signal quality and
forecast availability are visible

103
00:06:46,205 --> 00:06:51,487
so a reviewer can understand what the
score actually rests on.

104
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:57,431
Replay is accelerated: thirty historical
seconds advance per wall second at

105
00:06:57,431 --> 00:06:58,875
the default setting.

106
00:06:58,875 --> 00:07:04,166
This is historical simulation, not a
connected wearable or live hospital

107
00:07:04,166 --> 00:07:04,647
feed.

108
00:07:04,647 --> 00:07:09,457
Early decisions remain unavailable until
enough history and prior reliable

109
00:07:09,457 --> 00:07:10,900
baseline updates exist.

110
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:15,710
Warm-up is an explicit state, not a
missing zero-risk prediction.

111
00:07:15,710 --> 00:07:21,002
Watch the clock and availability reason
together as the recording advances.

112
00:07:21,655 --> 00:07:23,979
Pause holds the current position.

113
00:07:23,979 --> 00:07:28,629
Step advances one decision, which makes
changes easier to inspect.

114
00:07:28,629 --> 00:07:34,673
The forecast panel shows an issue time,
the future target interval and the

115
00:07:34,673 --> 00:07:36,067
frozen model version.

116
00:07:36,067 --> 00:07:41,646
Its percentage is a calibrated model
score, not an assurance of clinical

117
00:07:41,646 --> 00:07:42,111
probability.

118
00:07:42,111 --> 00:07:47,225
Quality acceptance alone does not
guarantee a forecast: history, warm-up and

119
00:07:47,225 --> 00:07:50,480
a loaded compatible model are also
required.

120
00:07:51,133 --> 00:07:55,684
The baseline stores earlier reliable
feature statistics and updates after

121
00:07:55,684 --> 00:07:56,139
prediction.

122
00:07:56,139 --> 00:08:01,145
Its movement does not mean the model is
learning new weights.

123
00:08:01,145 --> 00:08:06,606
For the real finalist it is contextual
state, not a predictor input.

124
00:08:06,606 --> 00:08:12,067
The evidence table lists large
contributions to the raw model score and

125
00:08:12,067 --> 00:08:15,253
compares available values with earlier
baseline context.

126
00:08:15,253 --> 00:08:20,259
These are model explanations, not causes
of AF and not treatment

127
00:08:20,259 --> 00:08:20,714
recommendations.

128
00:08:21,367 --> 00:08:25,456
Warnings require persistent elevated
scores under the configured policy.

129
00:08:25,456 --> 00:08:30,453
The record captures issue time, future
interval, model identity and feature

130
00:08:30,453 --> 00:08:30,907
evidence.

131
00:08:30,907 --> 00:08:36,813
A reviewer can mark it reviewed, dismissed
or pending and add a note.

132
00:08:36,813 --> 00:08:39,993
That action becomes part of persistent
history.

133
00:08:39,993 --> 00:08:45,899
Human review does not turn a false warning
into a correct prediction, and

134
00:08:45,899 --> 00:08:49,533
the software offers no diagnosis or
treatment decision.

135
00:08:50,186 --> 00:08:53,875
Manufactured patient zero has an
intentional unreliable stretch.

136
00:08:53,875 --> 00:08:58,486
Here we inspect the quality reason and
unavailable forecast together.

137
00:08:58,486 --> 00:09:03,097
Abstention means the system declines to
issue a usable score;

138
00:09:03,097 --> 00:09:06,786
it does not mean the patient is safe.

139
00:09:06,786 --> 00:09:11,397
In real-data evaluation, rejected time and
events missed during abstention

140
00:09:11,397 --> 00:09:12,319
remain visible.

141
00:09:12,319 --> 00:09:17,391
Otherwise a model could look better simply
by refusing the difficult

142
00:09:17,391 --> 00:09:17,852
periods.

143
00:09:18,506 --> 00:09:23,520
When no warning is issued, the interface
preserves that state without

144
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,888
inventing an alert.

145
00:09:24,888 --> 00:09:29,447
A low score or quiet warning list is not
reassurance.

146
00:09:29,447 --> 00:09:34,462
Reset restarts this patient's replay and
clears its warning and review

147
00:09:34,462 --> 00:09:34,917
history;

148
00:09:34,917 --> 00:09:36,741
pause merely stops progression.

149
00:09:36,741 --> 00:09:42,212
The saved state is useful for inspection,
but this synthetic example cannot

150
00:09:42,212 --> 00:09:43,579
establish clinical reliability.

151
00:09:44,233 --> 00:09:47,818
This evaluation screen is still
manufactured data.

152
00:09:47,818 --> 00:09:52,429
It exercises metric presentation,
calibration plots, misses and warning

153
00:09:52,429 --> 00:09:52,941
outcomes.

154
00:09:52,941 --> 00:09:58,576
Do not read these attractive demo numbers
as the project's real-data

155
00:09:58,576 --> 00:09:59,088
results.

156
00:09:59,088 --> 00:10:03,698
Those are the weak frozen evaluations we
show next.

157
00:10:04,352 --> 00:10:09,002
A separate saved real-development-prefix
receipt records seventy-two replay

158
00:10:09,002 --> 00:10:13,652
steps, median twenty-five milliseconds and
p ninety-five twenty-seven

159
00:10:13,652 --> 00:10:15,396
milliseconds per step.

160
00:10:15,396 --> 00:10:20,627
Future-only signal or annotation changes
left earlier outputs identical.

161
00:10:20,627 --> 00:10:26,440
That checks causal behavior and local
execution cost, not forecasting

162
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:29,347
usefulness or wearable hardware
performance.

163
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:34,470
Our evaluation starts with the unit of
independence.

164
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:39,048
Overlapping ECG windows from one person
share substantial physiological

165
00:10:39,048 --> 00:10:39,556
information.

166
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:45,152
Randomly mixing those windows between
training and testing would answer an

167
00:10:45,152 --> 00:10:48,713
easier question than generalization to
another person.

168
00:10:48,713 --> 00:10:53,291
We separate patient groups and preserve
their chronological streams,

169
00:10:53,291 --> 00:10:54,817
including negative-only recordings.

170
00:10:54,817 --> 00:10:58,887
Software success and model usefulness are
assessed separately.

171
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:03,876
Fitting, early-stopping, calibration and
policy roles are disjoint where

172
00:11:03,876 --> 00:11:05,324
those stages apply.

173
00:11:05,324 --> 00:11:10,635
Model weights, calibration and warning
policy were frozen before primary and

174
00:11:10,635 --> 00:11:11,601
external evaluation.

175
00:11:11,601 --> 00:11:17,395
Those cohorts have now been examined and
cannot be described as untouched

176
00:11:17,395 --> 00:11:19,326
for another tuning cycle.

177
00:11:19,326 --> 00:11:24,154
Fresh output directories and source-bound
receipts preserve what was run.

178
00:11:24,154 --> 00:11:28,983
Future model selection needs development
evidence and a fresh confirmation

179
00:11:28,983 --> 00:11:29,465
cohort.

180
00:11:30,109 --> 00:11:31,877
We replay whole recordings.

181
00:11:31,877 --> 00:11:37,181
Each warning can match at most one
eligible event within the inclusive

182
00:11:37,181 --> 00:11:41,159
two-to-ten-minute interval, and each event
can be matched once.

183
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:45,579
Missed events stay in sensitivity even
when every opportunity was

184
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:46,021
unavailable.

185
00:11:46,021 --> 00:11:49,557
Current AF, washout and unknown-outcome
warnings receive separate

186
00:11:49,557 --> 00:11:49,999
accounting.

187
00:11:49,999 --> 00:11:56,187
They must not disappear from the report
simply because they do not fit the

188
00:11:56,187 --> 00:11:57,513
primary assessment question.

189
00:11:58,156 --> 00:12:00,160
The denominator is crucial.

190
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:04,169
Assessed false warnings are divided by
labelled, forecast-eligible

191
00:12:04,169 --> 00:12:07,175
monitoring hours, including
quality-rejected eligible windows.

192
00:12:07,175 --> 00:12:13,688
Using all recorded hours would let unknown
or excluded time dilute the rate.

193
00:12:13,688 --> 00:12:16,194
Coverage is a separate quantity.

194
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:20,703
Event eligibility requires sufficient
labelled non-AF history, a minimum

195
00:12:20,703 --> 00:12:24,711
thirty-second episode, the target interval
and post-AF washout.

196
00:12:24,711 --> 00:12:31,225
Report both counts and rates so a small
denominator cannot hide behind a

197
00:12:31,225 --> 00:12:31,726
percentage.

198
00:12:32,369 --> 00:12:37,332
IRIDIA-AF contains one hundred and
sixty-seven recordings from one hundred

199
00:12:37,332 --> 00:12:42,791
and fifty-two patients, about six thousand
six hundred and ninety monitoring

200
00:12:42,791 --> 00:12:43,288
hours.

201
00:12:43,288 --> 00:12:49,243
Our development cohort has one hundred and
twenty-one patient groups and two

202
00:12:49,243 --> 00:12:51,725
hundred and forty-one eligible events;

203
00:12:51,725 --> 00:12:56,688
the frozen primary cohort has thirty-one
groups and forty-three events.

204
00:12:56,688 --> 00:13:00,658
LTAF contributes twenty-nine events across
eighty-four recording groups.

205
00:13:00,658 --> 00:13:05,125
Cross-record patient identity is
unverified there, so recording groups

206
00:13:05,125 --> 00:13:08,102
cannot simply be called independent
people.

207
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:14,242
Our operating assumptions are at most zero
point two five assessed false

208
00:13:14,242 --> 00:13:19,280
warnings per eligible hour and at least
fifty percent event sensitivity.

209
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:24,318
These are our research criteria, not a
clinical standard or organizer

210
00:13:24,318 --> 00:13:25,234
accuracy requirement.

211
00:13:25,234 --> 00:13:29,357
Passing one criterion cannot compensate
for failing the other.

212
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:33,292
These are the frozen finalist's results.

213
00:13:33,292 --> 00:13:35,703
The dashboard examples have ended.

214
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:40,694
Development caught six of two hundred and
forty-one events.

215
00:13:40,694 --> 00:13:44,556
The primary held-out cohort caught one of
forty-three.

216
00:13:44,556 --> 00:13:46,969
LTAF caught two of twenty-nine.

217
00:13:46,969 --> 00:13:52,761
Sensitivity is roughly two to seven
percent, far below our fifty percent

218
00:13:52,761 --> 00:13:53,244
target.

219
00:13:53,244 --> 00:13:57,105
Acceptance fails despite assessed
false-warning rates below budget.

220
00:13:57,105 --> 00:14:00,002
Most events receive no advance warning.

221
00:14:00,649 --> 00:14:07,173
Primary AUROC is zero point six one one,
and LTAF AUROC is zero point six

222
00:14:07,173 --> 00:14:08,043
three one.

223
00:14:08,043 --> 00:14:10,652
Ranking performance summarizes scores
across thresholds;

224
00:14:10,652 --> 00:14:16,741
it does not tell us how many events this
warning policy catches at the

225
00:14:16,741 --> 00:14:17,611
operating budget.

226
00:14:17,611 --> 00:14:20,655
The low event counts remain the headline.

227
00:14:21,303 --> 00:14:25,844
We independently compared saved score
timing with random within-record

228
00:14:25,844 --> 00:14:27,358
shifts, without refitting.

229
00:14:27,358 --> 00:14:32,403
Development observed six detections
against about four point five expected

230
00:14:32,403 --> 00:14:33,917
at random timing.

231
00:14:33,917 --> 00:14:38,963
The held-out cohorts together observed
three of seventy-two against about

232
00:14:38,963 --> 00:14:40,981
zero point seven expected.

233
00:14:40,981 --> 00:14:46,532
Only three events, intervals including
zero, and a post-hoc check cannot

234
00:14:46,532 --> 00:14:47,541
establish skill.

235
00:14:47,541 --> 00:14:50,568
We claim no demonstrated event-level
skill.

236
00:14:51,216 --> 00:14:53,426
LTAF illustrates the denominator problem.

237
00:14:53,426 --> 00:14:56,963
There were three hundred and ninety-eight
warning starts.

238
00:14:56,963 --> 00:15:01,384
Three hundred and ninety-two were
unassessable: two hundred and twenty-two

239
00:15:01,384 --> 00:15:05,804
during AF, seventy-seven in washout and
ninety-three in unknown time.

240
00:15:05,804 --> 00:15:08,457
Only four were assessed false warnings.

241
00:15:08,457 --> 00:15:13,762
Its zero point zero zero eight assessed
rate therefore needs the whole

242
00:15:13,762 --> 00:15:15,530
warning inventory beside it.

243
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:20,835
The same warning time placed randomly
gives about zero point one zero

244
00:15:20,835 --> 00:15:23,045
assessed false warnings per hour.

245
00:15:23,693 --> 00:15:25,865
Fusion also failed to help.

246
00:15:25,865 --> 00:15:30,211
The ECG-only reference caught seven
development events, compared with six

247
00:15:30,211 --> 00:15:32,384
for age, sex and ECG.

248
00:15:32,384 --> 00:15:37,598
Development Brier score was zero point
zero zero eight three eight four,

249
00:15:37,598 --> 00:15:43,247
versus zero point zero zero eight three
five eight for the observed constant

250
00:15:43,247 --> 00:15:44,116
base-rate reference.

251
00:15:44,116 --> 00:15:48,461
A smaller-looking probability error is not
sufficient when the reference

252
00:15:48,461 --> 00:15:49,765
performs as well.

253
00:15:50,413 --> 00:15:54,108
Other attempts included gradient boosting,
personal-baseline features,

254
00:15:54,108 --> 00:15:59,388
ectopy-like motifs, RR temporal CNNs
catching four and seven development

255
00:15:59,388 --> 00:16:05,196
events, a waveform CNN catching four while
occupying warning state about

256
00:16:05,196 --> 00:16:10,475
thirty-three percent of the time, and
precursor ranking catching five.

257
00:16:10,475 --> 00:16:13,115
ECGFounder produced no outcome fit;

258
00:16:13,115 --> 00:16:18,923
the last cloud job failed during
dependency setup before data reads.

259
00:16:18,923 --> 00:16:22,090
Engineering progress is not predictive
evidence.

260
00:16:22,738 --> 00:16:27,233
A development-fold calibration defect
reversed ranking from zero point five

261
00:16:27,233 --> 00:16:30,830
seven three to zero point four two seven.

262
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:34,426
Frozen finalists have positive slopes and
are unaffected.

263
00:16:34,426 --> 00:16:37,573
A later exploratory guard rejects
non-positive slopes;

264
00:16:37,573 --> 00:16:42,069
it does not repair history or change these
saved results.

265
00:16:42,716 --> 00:16:47,337
Published comparison claims use different
reporting and omit the operating

266
00:16:47,337 --> 00:16:49,186
false-alarm evidence we need.

267
00:16:49,186 --> 00:16:55,193
We therefore keep them as context, not
proof that our target is achievable.

268
00:16:55,193 --> 00:16:59,352
Closed attempts remain preserved, with
their failures and limitations.

269
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:03,031
The limits extend beyond sensitivity.

270
00:17:03,031 --> 00:17:08,293
These are retrospective public recordings,
not a prospective device study.

271
00:17:08,293 --> 00:17:14,082
There is no Indian-population evidence, no
secured clinical partner and no

272
00:17:14,082 --> 00:17:15,135
treatment advice.

273
00:17:15,135 --> 00:17:18,818
LTAF patient independence across records
is unverified.

274
00:17:18,818 --> 00:17:23,554
Development estimates follow exploration
across many candidates, and already

275
00:17:23,554 --> 00:17:28,290
examined test cohorts cannot supply a
fresh confirmation claim.

276
00:17:28,290 --> 00:17:33,026
Clinical metadata are limited, signal
preprocessing is source-specific, and

277
00:17:33,026 --> 00:17:37,236
RR variability is not automatically
validated normal-to-normal heart-rate

278
00:17:37,236 --> 00:17:37,763
variability.

279
00:17:37,763 --> 00:17:41,972
Local replay latency describes this
software and workload;

280
00:17:41,972 --> 00:17:47,761
it does not certify battery use, wireless
reliability or continuous wearable

281
00:17:47,761 --> 00:17:48,813
hardware performance.

282
00:17:48,813 --> 00:17:54,076
The dashboard's manufactured profiles must
remain visibly separate from real

283
00:17:54,076 --> 00:17:55,128
patient evidence.

284
00:17:55,768 --> 00:18:00,729
A future validation program would begin
with an ethically approved clinical

285
00:18:00,729 --> 00:18:03,886
partner and a clearly specified monitoring
setting.

286
00:18:03,886 --> 00:18:08,847
Before fitting a new model, declare the
target, patient roles, missing-data

287
00:18:08,847 --> 00:18:11,553
rules, warning budget and advancement
gates.

288
00:18:11,553 --> 00:18:15,613
Diagnose measurement and calibration
first, then compare against simple

289
00:18:15,613 --> 00:18:18,319
references on the same complete timelines.

290
00:18:18,319 --> 00:18:22,829
Preserve failed attempts rather than
silently change thresholds after seeing

291
00:18:22,829 --> 00:18:23,280
results.

292
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:28,692
If a model earns further study, use a
fresh prospective silent evaluation:

293
00:18:28,692 --> 00:18:33,653
log alerts without showing them to
clinicians, then assess events, false

294
00:18:33,653 --> 00:18:36,359
warnings, coverage and burden with
uncertainty.

295
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:41,320
Only later could a separate study examine
whether acting on warnings

296
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,222
improves care.

297
00:18:42,222 --> 00:18:45,830
None of those stages has been completed
here.

298
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:51,242
For this submission, the appropriate
action is to preserve the weak result

299
00:18:51,242 --> 00:18:56,203
and make the workflow inspectable,
reproducible and clear about what remains

300
00:18:56,203 --> 00:18:56,654
unmeasured.

301
00:18:56,654 --> 00:18:59,360
The acceptance gates remain research
assumptions.

302
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:05,374
The repository shown here is Lazarus, MGM,
Jawaharlal Nehru Engineering

303
00:19:05,374 --> 00:19:07,861
College, under sumitjadhav1703 on GitHub.

304
00:19:07,861 --> 00:19:12,834
It ships source, locked dependencies,
tests, selected evaluation reports and

305
00:19:12,834 --> 00:19:13,829
submission documents.

306
00:19:13,829 --> 00:19:19,300
Raw ECG, model binaries, local patient
state and private research receipts

307
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:20,295
are omitted.

308
00:19:20,295 --> 00:19:26,263
The recorded public test run on
seventeenth October had eight hundred and

309
00:19:26,263 --> 00:19:29,745
forty-one passes and eighty-three skips
without PyTorch;

310
00:19:29,745 --> 00:19:33,227
this is not a fresh test claim.

311
00:19:33,227 --> 00:19:37,703
The full canonical repository address
stays visible on screen.

312
00:19:37,703 --> 00:19:40,190
Data retain their own licences;

313
00:19:40,190 --> 00:19:42,179
code is MIT licensed.

314
00:19:42,815 --> 00:19:45,113
CardioTwin remains a research prototype.

315
00:19:45,113 --> 00:19:50,630
Its contribution is a causal replay
system, explicit evaluation gates and a

316
00:19:50,630 --> 00:19:52,469
documented negative forecasting result.

317
00:19:52,469 --> 00:19:57,066
A usable interface has not made the model
clinically useful.

318
00:19:57,066 --> 00:19:59,364
Thank you from Team Lazarus.
